bell Back Squat", 4, "6-8", 120, "exercise"], [3, 2, 2, "Leg Press", 4, "10-12", 120, "exercise"], [3, 2, 3, "Dumbbell Bulgarian Split Squat", 3, "8-10", 90, "exercise"], [3, 2, 4, "Leg Extension", 4, "12-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 2, 5, "Seated Leg Curl", 4, "10-12", 60, "exercise"], [3, 2, 6, "Standing Calf Raise", 4, "10-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 2, 7, "Kneeling Cable Crunch", 3, "10-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 4, 1, "Lat Pulldown", 4, "8-10", 120, "exercise"], [3, 4, 2, "Incline Dumbbell Press", 4, "8-10", 120, "exercise"], [3, 4, 3, "Dumbbell Single-Arm Row", 4, "10-12", 90, "exercise"], [3, 4, 4, "Cable Low-to-High Fly", 4, "12-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 4, 5, "Leaning Cable Lateral Raise", 4, "12-15", 0, "exercise"], [3, 4, 6, "Reverse Pec Deck", 3, "12-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 4, 7, "EZ-Bar Preacher Curl", 3, "8-10", 0, "exercise"], [3, 4, 8, "Overhead Cable Extension", 3, "8-10", 90, "exercise"], [3, 5, 1, "Romanian Deadlift", 4, "6-8", 120, "exercise"], [3, 5, 2, "Hip Thrust", 4, "8-10", 120, "exercise"], [3, 5, 3, "Smith Machine Squat", 3, "10-12", 90, "exercise"], [3, 5, 4, "Lying Leg Curl", 4, "10-12", 60, "exercise"], [3, 5, 5, "Hip Abduction", 3, "12-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 5, 6, "Seated Calf Raise", 4, "12-15", 60, "exercise"], [3, 5, 7, "Hanging Knee Raise", 3, "10-15", 60, "exercise"]]'::jsonb);
  perform pg_temp.add_program('Weight loss 3-week block', 'weekly', 3, 'For clients who want to lose fat while keeping their muscle. Every session trains the whole body with weights first, then finishes with 8-15 minutes of cardio intervals. Week 1 builds the habit, leaving 3 reps in the tank; week 2 adds finisher rounds and leaves 2; week 3 adds a set to the big lifts and leaves 1. Paired exercises with 0 rest are supersets. When you hit the top of the rep range on every set, add weight, because lifting heavy is what tells your body to keep its muscle. Walk 7,000-10,000 steps a day, sleep 7-9 hours, and take an easier week after week 3.',
    'Eat about 15-25% below maintenance so you lose 0.5-1% of bodyweight a week. Faster than that costs muscle. Protein is your priority: 1.8-2.4 g per kg of goal bodyweight a day, because it keeps you full and protects muscle. Fill half your plate with veg, a quarter with lean protein and a quarter with smart carbs, and keep fats around 0.6-0.8 g/kg. Simple swaps: grilled chicken, pap and chakalaka instead of a takeaway burger; egg-white and veg omelette instead of a pastry; biltong or a high-protein yoghurt instead of chips; cauliflower rice or extra veg instead of a second serving of rice. Drink 2.5-3 litres of water a day, and have a glass before each meal.', '4 minutes on the bike or treadmill, building to a light sweat. Then 1 round of 10 bodyweight squats, 10 glute bridges, 10 band pull-aparts and 10 hip hinges, and 1 light set of the first lift.',
